<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aghsu</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as New Shamakhi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aghsu is a town in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>, on the plain south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shamakhi">Shamakhi</a>. In 1734 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a> destroyed Shamakhi and moved its people to a new town here, known as New Shamakhi. In the 18th century it served alternately with Old Shamakhi as the capital of the Shirvan Khanate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aghsu.jpg" alt="Aghsu" width="320" height="569" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tərxan Paşazadə · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A%C4%9Fsu_pereval%C4%B1_3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
